  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The area bounded by the curves $x+2 y^{2}=0$ and $x+3 y^{2}=1$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "i9iNa",
      "text": "1 sq. unit",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yS9R4",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$ sq. units",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "o3Lez",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$ sq. units",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1qwdm",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$ sq. units",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $x+2 y^{2}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y^{2}=-\\frac{x}{2} \\ldots \\text { (i) }$\r\n\r\na parabola with vertex $(0,0)$ and $x+3 y^{2}=1$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y^{2}=\\frac{1-x}{3}=-\\left(\\frac{x-1}{3}\\right) \\ldots$ (ii), a parabola with vertex $(1,0)$\r\n\r\nSolving (i) and (ii), we get $y=\\pm 1$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/1uUb_Wysw315Rl0DFYCFG6Ly7ChrUi0sAteTJV3PPqo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{A}=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(\\left(1-3 y^{2}\\right)-\\left(-2 y^{2}\\right)\\right) d y$\r\n\r\n$=2 \\int_{0}^{1}\\left(1-y^{2}\\right) d y=2\\left[y-\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{4}{3}$ sq.units",
    "image": null
  },
